<section class="docs-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="section-kicker">Developer API</span>
    <h1 class="docs-title">Ask API</h1>
    <p class="docs-lead">
      Send a plain-English question. Querywell writes a read-only <code>SELECT</code>, runs it on the workspace database, and returns the SQL with the rows.
      Use the same monthly quota as SQL Studio.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-hero-meta">
      <span class="badge badge-indigo">POST /api/ask</span>
      <span class="badge badge-subtle">Bearer API key</span>
      <span class="badge badge-subtle">JSON or NDJSON</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="docs-body">
  <div class="wrap docs-layout">
    <aside class="docs-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="docs-toc-label">On this page</p>
      <a href="#auth">Authentication</a>
      <a href="#ask">POST /api/ask</a>
      <a href="#request">Request</a>
      <a href="#response">JSON response</a>
      <a href="#examples">Examples</a>
      <a href="#stream">Streaming</a>
      <a href="#errors">Errors</a>
      <a href="#limits">Limits</a>
    </aside>

    <div class="docs-content">
      <section id="auth" class="docs-section">
        <h2>Authentication</h2>
        <p>
          Create a key in <a href="/keys">API Keys</a>. Send it on every request. The key is shown once; after that only the prefix is stored.
        </p>
        <div class="code-box">
          <div class="code-box-header"><span>Header</span></div>
          <pre><code>Authorization: Bearer ask_live_…</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>
          Keys start with <code>ask_live_</code>. A workspace can have 10 active keys. A signed-in browser session also works, but scripts should use a key.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="ask" class="docs-section">
        <h2>POST /api/ask</h2>
        <p>
          The workspace must already have a connected, indexed MySQL database. The question is answered against that database.
        </p>
        <div class="docs-endpoint">
          <span class="docs-method">POST</span>
          <code class="docs-path">/api/ask</code>
        </div>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Header</th>
                <th>Value</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>Authorization</code></td>
                <td><code>Bearer</code> plus the API key</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>Content-Type</code></td>
                <td><code>application/json</code></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>Accept</code></td>
                <td><code>application/json</code> for one JSON object. Omit it, or send <code>application/x-ndjson</code>, for a stream of events.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="docs-note">
          Set <code>Accept: application/json</code> when you want the SQL in one response. Without that header the body is newline-delimited events, which is what SQL Studio uses.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="request" class="docs-section">
        <h2>Request body</h2>
        <div class="code-box">
          <div class="code-box-header"><span>JSON</span></div>
          <pre><code>{
  "question": "How many proposals were submitted last year?"
}</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Field</th>
                <th>Type</th>
                <th>Required</th>
                <th>Notes</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>question</code></td>
                <td>string</td>
                <td>Yes</td>
                <td>Plain English. Trimmed. 1–2000 characters.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>provider</code></td>
                <td>string</td>
                <td>No</td>
                <td><code>anthropic</code> for Claude, or <code>gemini</code> when <code>GEMINI_API_KEY</code> is set. Omitted requests use <code>SQL_PROVIDER</code>, which defaults to Claude.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="response" class="docs-section">
        <h2>JSON response</h2>
        <p>
          With <code>Accept: application/json</code>, a successful call returns <code>200</code> and the generated SQL in <code>sql</code>.
        </p>
        <div class="code-box">
          <div class="code-box-header"><span>200</span></div>
          <pre><code>{
  "question": "How many proposals were submitted last year?",
  "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM PROPOSAL WHERE YEAR(SUBMITTED_DATE) = YEAR(CURDATE()) - 1 LIMIT 100",
  "columns": ["n"],
  "rows": [{ "n": 142 }],
  "explanation": "Counts institutional proposals submitted in the previous calendar year.",
  "provider": "anthropic",
  "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
  "telemetry": {
    "schema_ms": 12,
    "synthesis_ms": 1840,
    "execution_ms": 31
  },
  "usage": {
    "used": 4,
    "limit": 30
  }
}</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Field</th>
                <th>Type</th>
                <th>Meaning</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>question</code></td>
                <td>string</td>
                <td>The question that was asked.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>sql</code></td>
                <td>string or null</td>
                <td>The <code>SELECT</code> that ran, including the result limit when Querywell added one.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>columns</code></td>
                <td>string[]</td>
                <td>Column names from the first row, or an empty list.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>rows</code></td>
                <td>object[]</td>
                <td>Query results. Dates are ISO-8601 strings. Empty when the statement returned no rows.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>explanation</code></td>
                <td>string</td>
                <td>Short reason for the SQL.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>provider</code></td>
                <td>string</td>
                <td><code>anthropic</code> or <code>gemini</code>, the model family that wrote the SQL.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>model</code></td>
                <td>string</td>
                <td>Model id, such as <code>claude-sonnet-4-6</code> or <code>gemini-3.8-flash</code>.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>telemetry</code></td>
                <td>object</td>
                <td>Schema, SQL generation, and execution time in milliseconds.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>usage</code></td>
                <td>object</td>
                <td>Successful questions used this month, and the plan limit.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="examples" class="docs-section">
        <h2>Examples</h2>
        <p>Replace the bearer token with a key from <a href="/keys">API Keys</a>. The host in these snippets is this site.</p>

        <div class="code-box">
          <div class="code-box-header">
            <span>curl</span>
            <button class="button button-sm ghost docs-copy" type="button" data-copy="#snippet-curl">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <pre><code id="snippet-curl">curl -sS __ORIGIN__/api/ask \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d "{\"question\":\"How many proposals were submitted last year?\"}"</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="code-box">
          <div class="code-box-header">
            <span>Python</span>
            <button class="button button-sm ghost docs-copy" type="button" data-copy="#snippet-python">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <pre><code id="snippet-python">import requests

response = requests.post(
    "__ORIGIN__/api/ask",
    headers={
        "Authorization": "Bearer YOUR_API_KEY",
        "Accept": "application/json",
    },
    json={"question": "How many proposals were submitted last year?"},
)
data = response.json()
print(data["sql"])
print(data["rows"])</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="code-box">
          <div class="code-box-header">
            <span>JavaScript</span>
            <button class="button button-sm ghost docs-copy" type="button" data-copy="#snippet-js">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <pre><code id="snippet-js">const response = await fetch("__ORIGIN__/api/ask", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: {
    Authorization: "Bearer YOUR_API_KEY",
    Accept: "application/json",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    question: "How many proposals were submitted last year?",
  }),
});
const data = await response.json();
console.log(data.sql);
console.log(data.rows);</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="stream" class="docs-section">
        <h2>Streaming</h2>
        <p>
          If <code>Accept</code> is missing or is <code>application/x-ndjson</code>, the response is <code>application/x-ndjson</code>: one JSON object per line.
        </p>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>step</th>
                <th>When</th>
                <th>Fields</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>status</code></td>
                <td>While the question is answered</td>
                <td><code>message</code></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>done</code></td>
                <td>After SQL runs</td>
                <td><code>sql</code>, <code>rows</code>, <code>explanation</code>, <code>used</code>, <code>limit</code>, timings</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>error</code></td>
                <td>If answering fails</td>
                <td><code>message</code></td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          Read lines until <code>done</code> or <code>error</code>. The SQL is on the <code>done</code> event, in <code>sql</code>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="errors" class="docs-section">
        <h2>Errors</h2>
        <p>JSON errors look like <code>{"error": "…"}</code>.</p>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Status</th>
                <th>When</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>400</code></td>
                <td>Missing or empty question, question longer than 2000 characters, or no indexed database on the workspace.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>401</code></td>
                <td>Missing or invalid API key, or no signed-in session.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>402</code></td>
                <td>The 14-day trial has ended.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>429</code></td>
                <td>The workspace has used its monthly question limit.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>502</code></td>
                <td>The model or database could not complete the question. The body is the public error message.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="limits" class="docs-section">
        <h2>Limits</h2>
        <ul class="docs-list">
          <li>Only a single <code>SELECT</code> is generated and run. Writes are rejected.</li>
          <li>Results are capped at 100 rows unless the SQL already has a <code>LIMIT</code>.</li>
          <li>Each successful answer counts against the workspace quota (30 on trial, then the paid plan limit).</li>
          <li>The connected MySQL user must be read-only. Querywell checks grants before it saves a connection.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Create keys in the app at <a href="/keys">/keys</a>, then call <code>POST /api/ask</code> with <code>Accept: application/json</code> to read <code>sql</code> and <code>rows</code>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
